In Day 1, you learned how Deployments ensure Pod count and how Services discover Pod IPs using 
EndpointSlices. Today, we dive into two critical production concepts:

Application-Level Health Checking: Preventing broken Pods from receiving traffic (Readiness) or
 restarting deadlock processes (Liveness).

Stateful Storage: Storing data so it survives Pod deletions and restarts using Persistent Volumes 
(PV) and Persistent Volume Claims (PVC).

With the fundamentals of workloads, configuration, and cluster networking completed, the next logical 
phase focuses on:

Container Probes & Health Checks: Implementing livenessProbe, readinessProbe, and startupProbe to automate 
endpoint routing and crash restarts.

Persistent Storage: Moving away from ephemeral storage using PersistentVolumes (PV), PersistentVolumeClaims (PVC),
 and dynamic StorageClasses.


